\contentsline {deleted}{Deleted: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{ They help loyal supporters feel seen and connected, but their ability to change minds or mobilize large numbers of previously disengaged young citizens is less clear. Paying attention to the contexts in which memes appear---their captions, comment threads, and the composition of the audiences that share them---thus helps to nuance claims about their impact. The negative effects that this paper has emphasized are most likely to be pronounced in dense, partisan online subcultures rather than evenly distributed across all young social media users.}}{4}{section*.47}%
